A||N||4||eagle01||starter problems||||1||
Z||000000||eagle01||08-03-2001||03:14 AM||||about a month back, when i start the car, sometimes, the starter would just spin but won't crank the engine. i would try a few more clicks and eventually, it would catch and crank and start the car.  last week though, it didn't catch at all.  the starter would just spin but wouldn't engage the flyweel (i have a v-6 manual).  so today, i went out and bought a new starter /solenoid, plugged it in and turned on the ignition.<BR>the starter just spins.  what's going on here? please help.  THANKS everyone!<P>Ed in Southern California ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-03-2001||10:26 AM||||When you pulled off the old starter, what did the teeth on the flywheel look like? It is possible that the teeth have been worn down to where they won't engage the Bendix.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||08-03-2001||02:45 PM||||If you just have a few teeth knocked out of the flywheel for whatever reason rather than the whole thing being worn down, what you can do is put the car in gear and move it a couple of feet. That should turn the flywheel enough to get some good teeth. If the whole thing is worn down (which it shouldn't be, it's not that old a car), then you probably won't be able to get it going until you replace the flywheel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-03-2001||02:47 PM||||Did you put the correct spacers in when you bolted the starter on?<P>Some starters come with a  flat spacer that the bolts go through.. if you installed it, and yours did not have one.. it wont grab at all because of the space difference..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fast85GT||08-03-2001||03:10 PM||||Check your connections also.  If you have bad wires or connections, you may not get enough current to throw the gear into place all the way.<P>------------------<BR>Jeremy H<BR>Black 1985 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||1
